Input: {"decision_time_ms": 1789862399999, "macro_contexts": {"D1": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "low", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1789775999999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["The 28 bars after the 2771.00 high overlap heavily and print stepping-down highs (2771.00 -> 2680.00 -> 2643.52); no price above 2771.00 exists in the window, so the recent structure is a two-sided range, not a continuing trend leg.", "Upside pushes inside the range have failed within one to three bars: 2680.00 (1789084800000) reversed to 2358.62 by 1789430400000, and 2609.02 (1789344000000) was followed by a bear bar closing 2397.10.", "The 2771.00 high is a single spike bar (1787270400000: open 2326.31, high 2771.00, low 2325.31, close 2515.30) that gave back most of its own range in the same session, which is weak trend follow-through.", "The decision bar's high of 2643.52 is still below the 2680.00 and 2771.00 range extremes, so the latest bull bar is a leg inside the range until acceptance above those levels is established."], "evidence_for": ["Higher-low chain since 1368.42 with no lower low, and the post-spike pullback holds roughly 19% above the 1974.46 pre-breakout range top (lowest post-breakout low 2357.18).", "The ~2357 floor was defended twice with bull closes (2391.94 at 1788307200000, 2397.10 at 1789430400000), consistent with a bull flag consolidation rather than distribution at the low.", "Three spike bars (1787097600000-1787270400000) moved from 1916.51 to 2771.00, and that spike has not been retraced back toward its origin; a spike is a legitimate trend start on this timeframe.", "The decision bar closes 2612.02, above the 2609.02 high of 1789344000000 and above the 2514.72 close of the 2680.00 spike bar, showing buyers still pressing the upper part of the range."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["Window opens at 2132.39 and declines for 16 bars to 1368.42 (bar 1780704000